Root cause analysis: The vulnerability occurs in the `extract_dents` function where user-controlled input (dent_node.name) is directly used to construct file paths without proper validation. This allows path traversal attacks when malicious UBIFS files contain specially crafted node names with sequences like "../../". The fundamental issue is the lack of path sanitization before joining the user-provided name with the base directory path.

